      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T00:36:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You list this patch since it exposed the problem, but isn\u0027t it really a problem with upstream commit 00e16c3d68fce504e880f59c9bdf23b2a4759d6d which didn\u0027t correctly implement the #else case (which you are replacing).\n\nShouldn\u0027t this be submitted upstream?",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "346fd9dc_ec7e74b5",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1896910
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T00:41:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e You list this patch since it exposed the problem, but isn\u0027t it really a problem with upstream commit 00e16c3d68fce504e880f59c9bdf23b2a4759d6d which didn\u0027t correctly implement the #else case (which you are replacing).\n\nIt is not a problem upstream because these functions are only used as function pointers and they have no direct callers, therefore stubbing them as NULL pointer works.\n\n\u003e \n\u003e Shouldn\u0027t this be submitted upstream?\n\nI did: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/4193aa1b-6836-08c0-58fd-5f53c66682da@gmail.com/\n\nhowever not feeling very confident that this will be accepted since this technically only affects Android at this point.",
      "parentUuid": "03352500_9b58c72e",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d59467a8_2fd8f6de",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T00:47:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In that case shouldn\u0027t we leave this code alone, and make the android-specific uses of these conditional under CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS?",
      "parentUuid": "346fd9dc_ec7e74b5",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58fb3804_8dfc614e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1896910
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T00:51:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is an option, however Jason was probably under the impression and maybe rightfully so that he could use these functions irrespective of CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS. Would you prefer that route?",
      "parentUuid": "d59467a8_2fd8f6de",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d314d0c5_0297f52f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:12:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I thought this was starting to sound familiar. This issue was found by kernelci for android12-5.10 and a few other branches and fixed with https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/q/Ifc7351f74470c87018770395af4b4f6096f0d73f. Let\u0027s cherry-pick that one here too (and now we\u0027ll make sure it\u0027s everywhere).\n\nNot sure why kernelci didn\u0027t encounter it with this branch (besides the obvious fact that !CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS wasn\u0027t tested the same way)",
      "parentUuid": "58fb3804_8dfc614e",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b0417cb_4becf7b2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:31:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. `android13-5.15` doesn\u0027t have the patch: \"Fixes: ca927bd22ad8 (\"ANDROID: cpu/hotplug: avoid breaking Android ABI by fusing cpuhp steps\")\" so it\u0027s slightly different (and this Fixes tag should be removed). The previous patch won\u0027t work for it.\n\nIt looks like the patch is only needed in the -lts branch afterall. (android13-5.10-lts too).",
      "parentUuid": "d314d0c5_0297f52f",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49deeda1_393f3e5f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:35:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "...and the mystery of why kernelci didn\u0027t find it is solved. The bug isn\u0027t in android13-5.15 and android13-5.15-lts is currently not covered by kernelci.",
      "parentUuid": "d314d0c5_0297f52f",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2723b83c_23f2ac3d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1402164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to keep the grotesque hack from the original commit in one place without spilling over its implications elsewhere, just change `random_and_perf_prepare_fusion()` to do something like:\n\n    int (*fn)(unsigned int cpu);\n    fn \u003d perf_event_init_cpu;\n    fn(cpu);\n    fn \u003d random_prepare_cpu;\n    fn(cpu);\n    return 0;\n\nAnd like this you keep this all contained in one place.",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b14cfc62_cb152521",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:31:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any reason not to to just do what we did for this in android12-5.10:\n```\n#ifdef CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS\n        perf_event_init_cpu(cpu);\n#endif\n```",
      "parentUuid": "2723b83c_23f2ac3d",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "03350a43_957f720c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1402164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:35:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Works too. It\u0027s just less general. The function pointer thing ensures that these functions are never called through a different method than how upstream does it.\n\n\tdiff --git a/kernel/cpu.c b/kernel/cpu.c\n\tindex eed8ad199001..fbcc2d64048e 100644\n\t--- a/kernel/cpu.c\n\t+++ b/kernel/cpu.c\n\t@@ -1683,14 +1683,24 @@ int __boot_cpu_id;\n\t /* Horrific hacks because we can\u0027t add more to cpuhp_hp_states. */\n\t static int random_and_perf_prepare_fusion(unsigned int cpu)\n\t {\n\t-\tperf_event_init_cpu(cpu);\n\t-\trandom_prepare_cpu(cpu);\n\t+\tint (*fn)(unsigned int cpu);\n\t+\tfn \u003d perf_event_init_cpu;\n\t+\tif (fn)\n\t+\t\tfn(cpu);\n\t+\tfn \u003d random_prepare_cpu;\n\t+\tif (fn)\n\t+\t\tfn(cpu);\n\t \treturn 0;\n\t }\n\t static int random_and_workqueue_online_fusion(unsigned int cpu)\n\t {\n\t-\tworkqueue_online_cpu(cpu);\n\t-\trandom_online_cpu(cpu);\n\t+\tint (*fn)(unsigned int cpu);\n\t+\tfn \u003d workqueue_online_cpu;\n\t+\tif (fn)\n\t+\t\tfn(cpu);\n\t+\tfn \u003d random_online_cpu;\n\t+\tif (fn)\n\t+\t\tfn(cpu);\n\t \treturn 0;\n\t }",
      "parentUuid": "b14cfc62_cb152521",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99dbae0d_042e3b5d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:43:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d prefer to use the same patch we\u0027ve already used for this on other branches. I don\u0027t see a reason to make the \"grotesque hack\" more complicated.",
      "parentUuid": "03350a43_957f720c",
      "revId": "f150b10367fbd9feddd1ac93d5953fde0ec96b9b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
